# sqrlly currently uses the local Claude Code adapter (ACP) as the only
# LLM transport — no API keys are required. The runtime authenticates
# against your local `claude` CLI session by spawning
# `npx @zed-industries/claude-code-acp`.
#
# This file remains in the tree so the secret resolver's lookup chain
# (env > .env > workflow YAML) keeps a documented anchor for any
# project-local secrets that workflows might need (e.g. a script node
# that calls out to a third-party service). Add them here as needed;
# the resolver picks them up by name with `resolve_secret("MY_KEY")`.
